So - the best way in our case to do categories
is to have a table listing all available categories,
but to store category heirarchies as a list at the entry level.

Therefore, the levels are indicated by how many items are in the list.

and the list can contain any number of items in the categories table, including duplicates.

This gives the most flexibility for how we wish to arrange our entries and our drilling down or having overarching umbrella categories, in our pie charts.

So that would be the best multi level approach.

So we only ever store top_category for each category, and never level.

